BBUUGGSS
     The rrmmlloocckk implementation is currently not optimized for single processor
     systems.

     rrmm__ttrryy__rrlloocckk() can fail transiently even when there is no writer, while
     another reader updates the state on the local CPU.

     The rrmmlloocckk implementation uses a single per CPU list shared by all rm‐
     locks in the system.  If rmlocks become popular, hashing to multiple per
     CPU queues may be needed to speed up the writer lock process.

